  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening capacities for Disaster Risk Reduction in Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Considered the fifth country most exposed to the risk of disasters in the world, Haiti recurrently faces natural risks which can be of hydrometeorological or geodynamic origin. Reports from the government of Haiti dated 2016 showed that nearly 98% of the Haitian population is exposed to at least two natural hazards such as earthquake, hurricane, flood, drought. The country has been hit by more than a hundred disasters between 1900 and 2021.
Ranked as the third country most affected by extreme weather events worldwide, Haiti is the Caribbean country with the highest number of disasters per square kilometer.
According to EM DAT data, Haiti has a cyclone vulnerability index of 12.9 out of 13. Which makes it the most vulnerable country of the small island states in the Caribbean region.</narrative>
  </description>
